    // surface). The weights were not that: a projector took no N.l at all, a point light 0.25 + N.l -- so a light
    // grazing or behind the surface (no diffuse in pass 15) weighed in: unblocked it diluted a real mover shadow
    // (lighter), blocked it darkened what pass 15 lights (the lobe). Now w = light x max(N.l, 0) for both kinds (the
    // smooth normal, as the lit pass shades); N.l <= 0: no weight, no rays.
    if (L.proj_origin.w > 0.5) g_mv_base = projDiffuse(L, -dot(lv, L.proj_axis.xyz), ptc.xy) * atten;
    else                       g_mv_base = L.color_falloff.rgb * atten;
